VeridianOS: QCoro acknowledges the private Qt modules it requests

QCoro's QtQuick and QML integration is built on Qt internals by design and
requests QuickPrivate and QmlPrivate. Qt then warns that the project is
tied to this Qt build ("This project is using headers of the QuickPrivate
module ..."), unless the project says it knows: KDE projects get that
from ECM's KDECMakeSettings (QT_NO_PRIVATE_MODULE_WARNING, "We use private
Qt modules in various places"), which QCoro does not use. QCoro now sets
it where it asks for those modules. (The coupling is real and handled:
the stack builds QCoro against the Qt it runs with.)

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -64,6 +64,10 @@
 endif()
 if (QCORO_WITH_QTWEBSOCKETS)
     list(APPEND REQUIRED_QT_COMPONENTS WebSockets)
+endif()
+if (QCORO_WITH_QTQUICK OR QCORO_WITH_QML)
+    # The QtQuick and QML integrations use Qt internals by design.
+    set(QT_NO_PRIVATE_MODULE_WARNING ON)
 endif()
 if (QCORO_WITH_QTQUICK)
     list(APPEND REQUIRED_QT_COMPONENTS Gui Quick QuickPrivate)
